## DEVICE MANAGEMENT (OBLIGATORIO)

### MUST detect device dinámicamente (NEVER hardcode)

```python
# ✅ CORRECTO - Detección dinámica
class Pipeline:
    def __init__(self, model_path: str):
        self.device = torch.device('cuda' if torch.cuda.is_available() else 'cpu')
        logger.info(f"Using device: {self.device}")

# ❌ INCORRECTO - Hardcoded
self.device = torch.device('cuda:0')  # Falla si no hay GPU
self.device = torch.device('cuda')    # Falla si no hay GPU
```

### MUST move tensors to device

```python
# ✅ CORRECTO
def preprocess(self, image):
    tensor = transforms.ToTensor()(image)
    tensor = tensor.unsqueeze(0)  # Add batch dimension
    tensor = tensor.to(self.device)  # Move to GPU/CPU
    return tensor

# ❌ INCORRECTO - Tensor en CPU, model en GPU
tensor = transforms.ToTensor()(image)
outputs = self.model(tensor)  # RuntimeError: Input type and device mismatch
```

### SHOULD log GPU info at startup

```python
@app.on_event("startup")
async def startup():
    global pipeline
    pipeline = Pipeline()
    
    if torch.cuda.is_available():
        logger.info(f"GPU: {torch.cuda.get_device_name(0)}")
        logger.info(f"CUDA Version: {torch.version.cuda}")
        logger.info(f"GPU Memory: {torch.cuda.get_device_properties(0).total_memory / 1e9:.2f} GB")
    else:
        logger.info("Running on CPU")
```

