## CHECKLIST DE MODEL LOADING

Cuando cargues un modelo PyTorch, verifica:

- [ ] `weights_only=True` (security)
- [ ] `model.eval()` mode
- [ ] Dynamic device detection (no hardcode)
- [ ] `.to(device)` para model y tensors
- [ ] `torch.no_grad()` durante inference
- [ ] CUDA cache cleaning después de batches
- [ ] Error handling para CUDA OOM
- [ ] Logging de device info

---

## ANTI-PATTERNS (PROHIBIDOS)

### ❌ NEVER:
- `weights_only=False` sin justificación documentada
- Hardcodear device (`cuda:0`)
- Olvidar `model.eval()`
- Olvidar `torch.no_grad()` durante inference
- Ignorar CUDA out of memory errors
- Cargar modelos a nivel de módulo (antes de `startup`)
- No limpiar CUDA cache en batch processing

---

## MONITORING (RECOMENDADO)

```python
def log_gpu_stats(self):
    if torch.cuda.is_available():
        logger.info(f"GPU Memory Allocated: {torch.cuda.memory_allocated() / 1e9:.2f} GB")
        logger.info(f"GPU Memory Reserved: {torch.cuda.memory_reserved() / 1e9:.2f} GB")
```

